    "1 Co",
    "1Co"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Now concerning the collection for the saints, as I have given order to the churches of Galatia, even so do ye.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 16:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Upon the first day of the week let every one of you lay by him in store, as God hath prospered him, that there be no gatherings when I come.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 16:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "And when I come, whomsoever ye shall approve by your letters, them will I send to bring your liberality unto Jerusalem.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 16:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "And if it be meet that I go also, they shall go with me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 16:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Now I will come unto you, when I shall pass through Macedonia: for I do pass through Macedonia.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 16:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "And it may be that I will abide, yea, and winter with you, that ye may bring me on my journey whithersoever I go.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 16:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "For I will not see you now by the way; but I trust to tarry a while with you, if the Lord permit.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 16:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "But I will tarry at Ephesus until Pentecost.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 16:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "For a great door and effectual is opened unto me, and there are many adversaries.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 16:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "Now if Timotheus come, see that he may be with you without fear: for he worketh the work of the Lord, as I also do.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 16:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Let no man therefore despise him: but conduct him forth in peace, that he may come unto me: for I look for him with the brethren.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 16:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "As touching our brother Apollos, I greatly desired him to come unto you with the brethren: but his will was not at all to come at this time; but he will come when he shall have convenient time.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 16:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Watch ye, stand fast in the faith, quit you like men, be strong.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 16:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "Let all your things be done with charity.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 16:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "I beseech you, brethren, (ye know the house of Stephanas, that it is the firstfruits of Achaia, and that they have addicted themselves to the ministry of the saints,)",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 16:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "That ye submit yourselves unto such, and to every one that helpeth with us, and laboureth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 16:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "I am glad of the coming of Stephanas and Fortunatus and Achaicus: for that which was lacking on your part they have supplied.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 16:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "For they have refreshed my spirit and yours: therefore acknowledge ye them that are such.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 16:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "The churches of Asia salute you. Aquila and Priscilla salute you much in the Lord, with the church that is in their house.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 16:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "All the brethren greet you. Greet ye one another with an holy kiss.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 16:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "The salutation of me Paul with mine own hand.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 16:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "If any man love not the Lord Jesus Christ, let him be Anathema Maranatha.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 16:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with you.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 16:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "My love be with you all in Christ Jesus. Amen.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 16:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:16:24"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
